.TH FLYPAGE 1 "2026-11-22" "flypage 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flypage \- import documents from a scanner's memory and turn them into searchable PDFs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flypage
.RB [ \-v ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.br
.B flypage \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flypage
detects a scanner with internal memory (for example an IRIScan Book) when it
is plugged in, copies its files, lets the user sort them into named folders,
and produces PDF files with an invisible OCR text layer (Tesseract, through
ocrmypdf).
.PP
PNG, JPEG and PDF files are accepted. The settings are stored in
.IR ~/.config/flypage/config.toml .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B settings
Open the settings window: scanner profiles, destination folders, OCR
languages, file name template and interface language.
.TP
.B daemon
Watch for configured scanners being plugged in. On a match, copy their files
and open the processing window. It is started at login by the
.I io.github.flypage.Daemon.desktop
autostart entry.
.TP
.BI "sort " DIRECTORY " \fR[\fB\-\-keep\-originals\fR]"
Open the processing window on the files of a folder. By default a file is
deleted once its PDF is created;
.B \-\-keep\-originals
keeps it.
.TP
.BI "import\-window " STAGING
Open the processing window on a folder of files imported by the daemon.
Used internally by
.BR "flypage daemon" .
.TP
.BI "process \-\-dest " DIR " \fR[\fB\-\-merge\fR] " FILE ...
Convert files to searchable PDFs in
.I DIR
without opening a window.
.B \-\-merge
makes one PDF from all files, in the order given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show debug messages.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/flypage/config.toml
User settings.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/flypage/
Imported files waiting to be processed, and thumbnails.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/flypage/pending-deletions.json
Deletions to do on a scanner the next time it is plugged in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ocrmypdf (1),
.BR tesseract (1)
